# Cloud Admin & Owner Task Inventory: LLDAP + OpenFGA + libcloud REST + Vault Architecture

## Overview

This document maps every recurring task that cloud administrators and cloud owners must perform within the described architecture, which comprises four interacting systems:

- **LLDAP** — lightweight LDAP server that acts as the identity source, issuing users and group/role memberships
- **OpenFGA** — fine-grained authorization server that controls access to every libcloud REST API endpoint
- **libcloud REST API** — multi-cloud provisioning abstraction layer that translates REST calls into provider-specific operations (AWS, GCP, Azure, Alibaba, Nutanix, etc.)
- **HashiCorp Vault** — secrets backend that stores per-provider credentials; Vault policies are bound to LLDAP-derived roles so that only authorised users can trigger provisioning that reaches the cloud

Tasks are segmented by **who** executes them (Cloud Owner vs Cloud Admin), **how** they are fulfilled (pre-scripted runbook vs on-demand developer work), and **which system layer** they touch.

***

## System Interaction Map

```
User Login
    │
    ▼
LLDAP (identity + group/role assignment)
    │  ← LDAP bind/search by libcloud REST
    ▼
OpenFGA (AuthZ check for each REST call)
    │  ← OIDC auth to OpenFGA
    ▼
libcloud REST API
    │  ← fetches cloud credentials from Vault at runtime
    ▼
HashiCorp Vault (dynamic/static secrets per provider)
    │  ← Vault policy tied to user role from LLDAP
    ▼
Cloud Providers (AWS, GCP, Azure, Alibaba, Nutanix…)
```

***

## Part 1 — Cloud Owner Tasks

The Cloud Owner has global administrative scope: they define the authorisation model, manage Vault root-level configuration, and govern the roles that everything else hangs off. Most of these tasks are **infrequent but high-impact**, and many should be pre-scripted as CLI runbooks.

### 1.1 Identity & Role Governance (LLDAP)

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Define LDAP group schema (group naming convention that maps to roles, e.g. `cloud-admin`, `cloud-owner`, `cloud-dev-aws`, `cloud-ro`) | One-off / per new provider | Developer pre-scripts LDAP schema; Owner approves |
| Create top-level groups / roles in LLDAP | Per new team or project | Pre-scripted: `lldap-cli group create` wrapper script |
| Assign users to groups (initial onboarding) | Per new hire / contractor | Pre-scripted onboarding runbook |
| Remove users from all groups (offboarding) | Per departure | Pre-scripted offboarding runbook (must also trigger Vault token revocation) |
| Rotate LLDAP admin credentials | Quarterly / as needed | Pre-scripted Vault-backed rotation script |
| Audit group memberships | Monthly | Pre-scripted report script querying LDAP `memberOf` |

LLDAP exposes a GraphQL API and a web UI; group and user management can be automated via the GraphQL endpoint, making it straightforward to wrap in scripts.[1][2]

### 1.2 Authorization Model Governance (OpenFGA)

OpenFGA authorization models are **immutable** — every change creates a new model version with a new model ID, which must be pinned in libcloud REST's configuration.[3]

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Define or revise the authorization model (which roles can call which REST endpoints, with what conditions) | Per new API surface / per policy change | Developer work — model written in FGA DSL, reviewed by Owner |
| Publish new model version and pin new `authorization_model_id` in libcloud REST config | Per model change | Developer + Owner: model PR → CI pipeline publishes to OpenFGA store → config updated |
| Write/delete relationship tuples when new users/roles become active (e.g. `user:alice` has `role:cloud-admin`) | Per onboarding/offboarding | Pre-scripted: triggered by LLDAP group-change webhook or reconciliation cron |
| Audit relationship tuples in the FGA store | Monthly / post-incident | Pre-scripted: `fga tuple read` sweep; results compared to LLDAP ground truth |
| Shadow-check new model against production traffic before full rollout | Per model migration | Developer work — shadow check using dual model IDs[3] |
| Rotate OpenFGA preshared keys | Quarterly | Pre-scripted: update key in Vault → rolling restart of libcloud REST → update OpenFGA config[4][5] |
| Disable the OpenFGA playground on non-local environments | One-off at deployment | Infrastructure config (Terraform/Helm) — set `playground.enabled: false`[6] |

### 1.3 Vault Root Configuration (Secrets & Policy Governance)

Vault policies are the binding layer between LLDAP roles and cloud credentials.[7][8]

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Define and write Vault policies per role (e.g. policy `cloud-admin-aws` allows `read` on `aws/creds/admin-role`) | Per new role or provider | Developer writes HCL policy; Owner approves and applies via `vault policy write` |
| Bind Vault policies to LDAP groups using the Vault LDAP auth method | Per new role | Pre-scripted: `vault write auth/ldap/groups/<group> policies=<policy>` |
| Enable and configure cloud secrets engines (AWS, Azure, GCP, Alibaba) with root credentials | Per new provider onboarding | Developer work — one-off per provider; credentials stored out-of-band |
| Define Vault roles per cloud provider + permission level (e.g. `aws/roles/ec2-admin`, `aws/roles/ec2-readonly`) | Per new capability needed | Developer work; IAM policy documents authored per provider[9] |
| Rotate root credentials for each cloud secrets engine | Quarterly | Pre-scripted: `vault write <engine>/config/rotate-root` |
| Revoke all leases for a departing user or compromised credential | Immediate / per incident | Pre-scripted: `vault lease revoke -prefix <path>/` [10] |
| Audit Vault audit logs for anomalous secret access | Weekly / per alert | Pre-scripted: log pipeline to SIEM; Owner reviews anomaly dashboard |
| Unseal Vault after restart (if not using auto-unseal) | Per restart | Operational runbook with quorum of key holders |

***

## Part 2 — Cloud Admin Tasks

Cloud Admins operate within the policy envelope that the Owner has defined. Their daily work is provisioning, access management, and incident response — most of which should be exposed as pre-scripted commands that call libcloud REST, with Vault credential injection happening transparently.

### 2.1 User Lifecycle Management (LLDAP-driven)

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Add a new user to LLDAP (create account, set password) | Per onboarding | Pre-scripted onboarding script (LLDAP GraphQL `createUser` mutation) |
| Assign user to one or more role-groups in LLDAP | Per onboarding / role change | Pre-scripted: `lldap-cli group add-member` wrapper |
| Remove user from groups / disable account | Per offboarding or suspension | Pre-scripted offboarding runbook — must also delete OpenFGA tuples and revoke Vault tokens |
| Reset a user's LLDAP password | On request | Pre-scripted self-service reset or admin-initiated via LLDAP GraphQL |
| List users in a group (access review) | Monthly | Pre-scripted LDAP query / LLDAP API report |

### 2.2 Access Control — OpenFGA Tuple Management

Relationship tuples in OpenFGA represent the live state of "who can do what". Every time a user gains or loses a role, tuples must be written or deleted.[11]

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Write access tuple when user joins a role (e.g. `user:alice` → `member` of `role:cloud-admin`) | Per onboarding / role change | Pre-scripted: triggered by LLDAP group change; reconciliation job writes `WriteTuples` call to OpenFGA[11] |
| Delete access tuple when user leaves a role | Per offboarding / role change | Pre-scripted: same reconciliation job, calls `DeleteTuples` |
| Grant temporary elevated access (break-glass) for a specific resource | On demand | Pre-scripted: timed tuple write + scheduled deletion (developer builds the scheduler; admin invokes) |
| Verify access before a provisioning action (dry-run check) | On demand | Pre-scripted: `fga check user:<id> <relation> <object>` wrapper |
| List all objects a user has access to | On demand / audit | Pre-scripted: `fga list-objects` for the user[11] |
| List all users who have access to a specific resource | Audit / periodic | Pre-scripted: `fga list-users` query |

### 2.3 Cloud Provisioning via libcloud REST

These are the **core day-to-day operational tasks** — all routed through the libcloud REST API, with credentials sourced from Vault and authorization checked by OpenFGA on each call.[12][13]

#### Compute

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| List available regions, instance sizes, and images for a provider | On demand | Pre-scripted: `GET /compute/{provider}/sizes`, `/images` |
| Provision a new VM / compute instance | On demand (user request) | Pre-scripted template-based script (size, image, region, SSH key as parameters) |
| Start / stop / reboot an existing node | On demand | Pre-scripted: `POST /compute/{provider}/nodes/{id}/action` |
| Destroy / delete a node | On demand | Pre-scripted: destructive action with confirmation prompt |
| List all running nodes and their state | Daily / on demand | Pre-scripted: `GET /compute/{provider}/nodes` |
| Resize / change instance type | On demand (user request) | Developer builds resize workflow (provider-specific steps vary) |
| Attach/detach storage volumes | On demand | Developer builds as provider-specific operations differ |
| Manage SSH key pairs (upload, list, delete) | Per project setup | Pre-scripted: `POST /compute/{provider}/keypairs` |
| Manage security groups / firewall rules | On demand | Developer work — security rules require review workflow |

#### Storage

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Create / delete object storage buckets or block volumes | On demand | Pre-scripted with naming-convention enforcement |
| Upload / download objects | On demand | Pre-scripted or exposed via libcloud REST endpoints |
| List buckets and their metadata | Daily / on demand | Pre-scripted reporting script |
| Configure bucket lifecycle policies | Per project | Developer builds policy template runner |

#### Networking (provider-dependent)

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| List available VPCs, subnets, and zones | On demand | Pre-scripted: `GET /network/{provider}/...` |
| Allocate / release floating IPs | On demand | Pre-scripted |
| Manage load balancer instances | On demand | Developer work — LB config is complex and provider-specific |
| DNS record management | On demand | Developer work — DNS changes have broad impact, need review |

### 2.4 Vault Credential Operations (Day-to-Day)

Admins interact with Vault indirectly (libcloud REST calls Vault internally), but some operational tasks are Admin-facing.[9][10]

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Verify Vault is reachable and unsealed | Daily (health check) | Pre-scripted: `vault status` health probe in monitoring |
| Renew a long-lived token before expiry (if service tokens are used) | Before TTL expiry | Pre-scripted: automated renewal job (Vault Agent or cron)[10][14] |
| Revoke a specific dynamic credential lease immediately after incident | Per incident | Pre-scripted: `vault lease revoke ease_id>`[10] |
| Request a manual dynamic credential for a one-off operation | On demand | Pre-scripted: `vault read <engine>/creds/<role>` — credential is time-bound |
| View active leases for a path | On demand / audit | Pre-scripted: `vault list sys/leases/lookup/<path>`[15] |
| Rotate a static secret stored in Vault (e.g. API key for a SaaS integration) | Quarterly / on trigger | Pre-scripted rotation runbook |

### 2.5 Observability & Incident Response

| Task | Frequency | Fulfillment |
|------|-----------|-------------|
| Review OpenFGA authorization denial logs for unexpected blocks | Daily | Pre-scripted: log query / alert rule |
| Investigate why a user's API call was denied (trace through OpenFGA → LLDAP → Vault) | On demand (incident) | Pre-scripted diagnostic script: checks tuple existence → checks LLDAP group → checks Vault policy |
| Review Vault audit logs for anomalous credential access patterns | Weekly | Pre-scripted: log pipeline to SIEM |
| Check libcloud REST API error rates per provider | Daily | Pre-scripted: metrics dashboard (Prometheus/Grafana or similar) |
| Respond to a Vault lease expiry that caused a provisioning failure | On incident | Runbook: identify lease, renew or request new credential, retry operation[10] |

***

## Part 3 — Developer-Built Components (Non-Scriptable Demand Work)

The following tasks **cannot be pre-scripted** because they depend on user intent, new business requirements, or provider-specific complexity. Developers must build these as new features or workflows.

| Capability | Reason Requires Developer | Systems Involved |
|------------|---------------------------|-----------------|
| New cloud provider onboarding | Requires: new libcloud driver integration, new Vault secrets engine config, new OpenFGA relations for provider-specific resources, new LLDAP groups | All four systems |
| New resource type support (e.g. managed Kubernetes, serverless, databases) | libcloud REST must expose new endpoints; OpenFGA model must define new relations; Vault may need new dynamic secret roles | libcloud REST + OpenFGA + Vault |
| Multi-cloud topology provisioning (VMs across providers in one request) | Requires orchestration logic, distributed rollback, cross-provider dependency resolution | libcloud REST (new composite endpoint) |
| Budget and quota enforcement per team/role | Requires a new policy layer querying cost APIs + blocking provisioning if threshold exceeded | libcloud REST + OpenFGA condition model |
| Automated resource expiry / TTL-based deprovisioning | Requires scheduler, state tracking, grace-period notification, and deprovisioning workflow | libcloud REST + new state store |
| Self-service provisioning portal / UI | Full frontend + backend work; inputs become libcloud REST API calls | All systems |
| Change approval workflow (request → approve → provision) | Requires workflow engine, notification integration, audit trail | libcloud REST + OpenFGA (approval relation) |
| Cost tagging and FinOps metadata enforcement | Provider-specific tag injection at create time; tag policy engine | libcloud REST |
| Audit export and compliance reporting | Aggregation of LLDAP audit, OpenFGA logs, Vault audit logs, and cloud provider CloudTrail/Activity logs into a unified report | Cross-cutting |
| OpenFGA model migration for a breaking change | Requires shadow-check harness, tuple migration script, progressive rollout with dual model IDs[3] | OpenFGA + libcloud REST config |
| Vault dynamic secrets for a new provider (e.g. Alibaba, Nutanix) | Provider-specific Vault plugin or custom secrets engine may need development | Vault + libcloud REST |
| Break-glass access with time-bound escalation | Timed tuple write + auto-delete in OpenFGA; Vault policy elevation + automatic revocation[10] | OpenFGA + Vault |

***

## Part 4 — Synchronisation & Consistency Concerns

Because identity lives in LLDAP, authorization state lives in OpenFGA, and access policy lives in Vault, the systems can drift. The following reconciliation jobs should be built and scheduled by developers, then monitored by admins.

| Job | Purpose | Trigger |
|-----|---------|---------|
| LLDAP → OpenFGA reconciler | Compare LLDAP group memberships to OpenFGA tuples; write missing tuples, delete stale ones | Scheduled cron (e.g. every 5 min) + on LLDAP group-change event |
| LLDAP → Vault LDAP auth sync | Ensure Vault's `auth/ldap/groups` mappings match current LLDAP groups | Scheduled cron; alert on mismatch |
| OpenFGA stale tuple sweep | Identify tuples referencing users or roles that no longer exist in LLDAP | Daily cron |
| Vault lease expiry monitoring | Alert before critical leases expire; trigger renewal or notify dependent service | Vault Agent or external monitor[10][14] |
| Dead-letter queue for failed provisioning | Capture libcloud REST calls that failed due to auth errors (FGA deny, Vault lease expiry) for admin review | libcloud REST middleware |

***

## Part 5 — Role-Responsibility Matrix

| Task Category | Cloud Owner | Cloud Admin | Developer (pre-build) |
|---------------|------------|-------------|----------------------|
| LLDAP schema & group design | ✅ Approves | ✅ Executes | ✅ Scripts |
| User onboarding/offboarding | ✅ Governs | ✅ Executes | ✅ Scripts |
| OpenFGA model design | ✅ Approves | — | ✅ Builds |
| OpenFGA tuple management | ✅ Governs | ✅ Executes | ✅ Scripts |
| Vault policy authoring | ✅ Approves | — | ✅ Builds |
| Vault LDAP group binding | ✅ Executes | — | ✅ Scripts |
| Cloud provider secrets engine setup | ✅ Executes | — | ✅ Builds |
| Vault credential revocation | ✅ Executes | ✅ Executes (scoped) | ✅ Scripts |
| Cloud provisioning (compute/storage/network) | — | ✅ Executes | ✅ Scripts |
| Observability & log review | ✅ Governs | ✅ Executes | ✅ Builds dashboards |
| New provider / resource type onboarding | ✅ Approves | — | ✅ Builds entirely |
| Reconciliation jobs | ✅ Governs | ✅ Monitors | ✅ Builds |
| Break-glass access | ✅ Approves | ✅ Invokes | ✅ Builds mechanism |
